Business Requirements Document
Smart Honeypot Orchestrator & Threat Intelligence Dashboard



1. Project Overview
Brief Description
The project aims to build a centralized platform for deploying and managing multiple honeypots. These honeypots act as fake vulnerable services that attract attackers and record their activities.
The collected attack data is then analyzed and displayed through a dashboard to help security teams understand attacker behavior, identify attack trends, and monitor threats in real time.
Business Context
Organizations face cyber-attacks on a daily basis. Security teams need stronger visibility into attacker activity in order to improve monitoring, detection, and response.
Background
Honeypots are decoy systems designed to attract and trap attackers. They allow organizations to safely study attack methods, attacker tools, and behavior patterns, improving overall security awareness without risking production systems.

2. Business Problem / Opportunity
Problem
Security teams often have limited visibility into attacker behavior and may only detect an intrusion after it has already reached real systems.
Opportunity
The project enables organizations to collect attack data in a safe, isolated environment, improving early threat visibility and supporting better-informed security decisions.

3. Business Objectives
•	Collect real-world attack data from deployed honeypots.
•	Monitor attacker activity and behavior in near real time.
•	Display attack data clearly on a centralized dashboard.
•	Identify common attack patterns and trends across sessions.

